				}
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "5B0DC9CA6B4CCB9E"
					item: "powergrid:copper_coil"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "1E18B210CD05D70D"
					item: "powergrid:generator_housing"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Generator Parts"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"2F195E8394E1BF22"
				"4DE094DCD88E1C78"
			]
			description: [
				"Right-click two shafts with a Copper Coil to create a winding. Windings around the rotor provide the magnetic field; adjacent windings can connect in series."
				""
				"Keep the first build small. The default config caps rotor assemblies at 8 blocks, and a small generator is easier to tune safely."
			]
			icon: "powergrid:copper_coil"
			id: "6030354EA9045463"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6CFB5BEAC30668CD"
				title: "Create generator windings"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Wind the Field"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 10.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The first practical generator is a shunt generator. It is self-excited, produces a mostly steady voltage once wired correctly, and can start from the residual magnetic field in the windings."
				""
				"Put adjustable resistance in series with the field windings. Lower resistance increases field current and voltage; higher resistance lowers it. Watch a Voltage Gauge while tuning."
			]
			icon: "powergrid:rheostat"
			id: "63F35AEE9852F86D"
			shape: "square"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6559713013D58C17"
				title: "Build and tune a shunt generator"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Shunt Generator"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 12.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["63F35AEE9852F86D"]
			description: [
				"The Battery stores electricity and changes behavior as it discharges. Use it as a buffer while you test real machines, not as a replacement for enough generation."
				""
				"A buffer gives short spikes somewhere to go, but sustained Mekanism loads still need enough generator power."
			]
			icon: "powergrid:battery"
			id: "5664E5E262521DFE"
			tasks: [{
				id: "40DACEEEBC0E8FDA"
				item: "powergrid:battery"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Grid Buffer"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 14.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["63F35AEE9852F86D"]
			description: [
				"Long wires lose power as heat. For distance, transmit at higher voltage and lower current, then step back down near the load."
				""
				"Grounding Rods provide a 0V reference, but they are not a magic return wire. Bad grounding conditions can electrify the area around the rod."
			]
			icon: "powergrid:transformer_core"
			id: "452C27666F7AD48F"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "1663D09D909C2F84"
					item: "powergrid:transformer_core"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "455357C254912AEE"
					item: "powergrid:heavy_wire_connector"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "1BC46F17BFC70DF0"
					item: "powergrid:grounding_rod"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Transmission Tools"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 14.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["63F35AEE9852F86D"]
			description: [
				"The Device Connector is the bridge to Forge Energy. Place it so its output face points into a block that can receive FE, such as a Mekanism cable or machine, then wire its electrical terminals into your Power Grid loop."
				""
				"In this world, the default conversion is 2 FE/t of buffer and transfer rate per volt, while the electrical cost is based on 10 FE per watt. More voltage raises the possible FE/t, but the generator still has to supply the watts."
			]
			icon: "powergrid:device_connector"
			id: "160D0503EE704DC1"
			tasks: [{
				id: "526A6E086B6CDE7E"
				item: "powergrid:device_connector"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Forge Energy Bridge"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 16.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["160D0503EE704DC1"]
			description: [
				"Now connect the Device Connector into Mekanism. A short Universal Cable run is a good first target because it lets you branch into several machines later."
				""
				"If the Mekanism machine flickers or drains faster than it fills, watch the Voltage and Power Gauges. Add generator capacity or reduce field resistance until the voltage stays stable under load."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_universal_cable"
